It is Sunday morning and I am in the flat.
Mostly I sleep late on Sundays.
I make a cozy breakfast with two bread rolls and a coffee.
Then I take the U-Bahn to a flea market.
The summer weather is warm and sunny.
The flea market is very crowded.
I see a lot of old things and clothes.
A seller has a beautiful coffee cup.
It costs three euros.
Normally I pay for everything with the card.
But here everyone pays in cash.
I give the seller three euros.
I do not get a till receipt here, of course.
I pack the cup into my backpack.
On the way home I am sitting in the U-Bahn again.
My mobile phone vibrates.
It is a short notification from the transit portal.
The text is very official:
"Your new email address was saved."
I read the sentence once and put the mobile phone away again.
